[D] Controller edits / agent access
UI commands
Agent bridge
+ register -> poll -> handle -> reply
+ live selections over WebSocket
MappingPage.handleAgentCommand
+ context -> version + nodes + edges
+ snapshot -> state + exported history
+ apply -> cached requestId receipt
MappingDocumentController
+ applyUpdate(expectedVersion, operations) <- transact MCP adapter
+ version match + 1..100 operations -> clone -> stage in order
Content operations
+ create / insert
+ replace / patch
+ mappings / jumps
+ apply revision
Document operations
+ edges create/update
+ edges remove
+ group / remove
+ delete-diagrams
Presentation operations
+ grid move -> cells
+ floating move -> pixels
+ collapse box or subtree
+ remove floating subtree
DiagramService
+ revise staged base
+ track node IDs
Grid layout
+ update + push right
+ validate anchors
DisplayState / diagramViews
+ normalize folded views
+ resolve floating geometry
patch -> rebase edge anchors, jumps, sections and collapsed node IDs
History commit
+ updateSnapshot -> append(document, canvas, correspondence)
+ refresh issued diagram references -> checkpoint + version -> subscribers
+ CanvasSession publishes stores; nodes() returns cloned read projection
+ select() records; updateCanvas() defaults to unrecorded
+ layout / endpoint measurements do not advance history
+ apply-diagram-revision via receiver -> persistence.sync -> storage.flush
+ copy-document -> fork history; clear selection/controls + pending chat

edge "UI commands" -> "MappingDocumentController"
edge "MappingPage.handleAgentCommand" -> "MappingDocumentController"
edge "Agent bridge" -- "MappingPage.handleAgentCommand"
edge "MappingDocumentController" -> "Content operations"
edge "MappingDocumentController" -> "Document operations"
edge "MappingDocumentController" -> "Presentation operations"
edge "Content operations" -> "DiagramService"
edge "Document operations" -> "Grid layout"
edge "Presentation operations" -> "DisplayState / diagramViews"
edge "patch -> rebase edge anchors, jumps, sections and collapsed node IDs" -> "History commit"
